From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: exynos5: Reset the controller stuck on an address

The master can be left in HSI2C_MASTER_ST_ADDR1, in the middle of sending
an address, and it does not leave that state on its own.  It does not clear
on the next transfer either: every following one ends immediately, so a
device that is present and answering looks absent.

Measured on a Galaxy S10+.  Its touchscreen answers a scan that resets the
block before each address and is not found at all without one, and reading
its registers through the driver fails with -ENXIO until the controller is
reset.  With the reset below the same registers read back the device ID and
a boot status of "application".

The state is already read here for the arbitration-lost check, so this
costs nothing but the comparison.  The vendor driver does the same, under a
samsung,reset-before-trans property, and keys it off the same value.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
index 20f8d4af6c2..4b7d99f7e7b 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
@@ -689,6 +689,20 @@ static void exynos5_i2c_bus_check(struct exynos5_i2c *i2c)
 	if (i2c->variant->hw == I2C_TYPE_EXYNOS5)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * HSI2C_MASTER_ST_ADDR1 state before a transaction means the master
+	 * never finished the previous one and stayed in the middle of sending
+	 * an address.  It does not recover on its own and it does not clear on
+	 * the next transfer either: every following one ends immediately, so
+	 * the device on the bus looks absent.  Measured on a Galaxy S10+, whose
+	 * touchscreen answers a scan that resets the block before each address
+	 * and is not found at all without it.  A reset of the controller is
+	 * what the vendor does here too.
+	 */
+	if ((readl(i2c->regs + HSI2C_TRANS_STATUS) & HSI2C_MASTER_ST_MASK) ==
+	    HSI2C_MASTER_ST_ADDR1)
+		exynos5_i2c_reset(i2c);
+
 	/*
 	 * HSI2C_MASTER_ST_LOSE state (in Exynos7 and ExynosAutoV9 variants)
 	 * before transaction indicates that bus is stuck (SDA is low).
